.TH SDE-UPDATE 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-update \- review and install system updates on DebION GNU/Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-update
[\fB--page\fR \fINAME\fR]
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--check\fR | \fB--history\fR | \fB--sources\fR
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--plan\fR \fIACTION\fR [\fIPACKAGE\fR...]
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--transaction\fR \fBrefresh\fR|\fBupgrade\fR
.br
.B sde-update
\fB--notifier\fR [\fB--once\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDE Update shows the updates in the local APT cache, grouped by source package
and by type: security, kernel, software and backports. The read-only Python APT
model is adapted from Linux Mint's Update Manager (mintupdate) with its original
GPLv3+ copyright preserved; held packages are excluded and counted.
.PP
The \fBUpdates\fR page shows the overall status, the download size and the time
of the last refresh, a searchable and filterable list with check boxes, and a
details pane with the installed and new versions, the packages of the group, the
origin and the changelog (\fBapt-get changelog\fR, then PackageKit's update
details, then the installed changelog), loaded in the background with a time
limit. A banner appears when \fI/run/reboot-required\fR exists.
.PP
\fBHistory\fR lists the transactions recorded in \fI/var/log/apt/history.log\fR
and its rotated copies. \fBSources\fR lists the entries of
\fI/etc/apt/sources.list\fR and \fI/etc/apt/sources.list.d\fR (one-line
\fI.list\fR and deb822 \fI.sources\fR files) read-only, and opens
software-properties-gtk when it is installed. \fBMaintenance\fR refreshes the
package lists, cleans the package cache, removes unused packages after showing
them, repairs interrupted installations and opens PackageKit's interactive
update in a terminal. \fBSettings\fR controls the automatic checks.
.PP
Transactions run in a helper process and report per-package progress. They use
PackageKit (\fBpkcon\fR) when its daemon is available, which applies the
system's polkit policy and can be cancelled; otherwise, and for cleaning and
removing unused packages, \fBapt-get\fR runs through \fBpkexec\fR. SDE Update
never runs APT as root by itself, accepts no repository URLs or options, and
validates every package name.
.PP
Debian testing transitions can require manual APT decisions; a preview from the
local cache does not guarantee that every upgrade is currently resolvable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --page " NAME"
Open \fBupdates\fR, \fBhistory\fR, \fBsources\fR, \fBmaintenance\fR,
\fBsettings\fR or \fBabout\fR.
.TP
.B --check
Print the versioned tab-separated update list (SDE-UPDATES 2) and exit.
.TP
.B --history
Print the APT history (SDE-HISTORY 1) and exit.
.TP
.B --sources
Print the package sources (SDE-SOURCES 1) and exit.
.TP
.BI --plan " ACTION" " " [PACKAGE...]
Print the fixed argument vector of \fBrefresh\fR, \fBupgrade\fR,
\fBautoremove\fR, \fBclean\fR or \fBrepair\fR without running it.
.TP
.B --transaction refresh|upgrade
Run the interactive PackageKit operation in the current terminal.
.TP
.B --notifier \fR[\fB--once\fR]
Check for updates in the background and show a notification. Started at login
from \fI/etc/xdg/autostart/sde-update-notifier.desktop\fR; \fB--once\fR checks
immediately and exits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The \fB[update]\fR section of \fIsde.conf\fR:
.TP
.B check_interval
Hours between automatic checks: 0 (never), 1, 6, 12, 24 or 168.
.TP
.B auto_refresh
Refresh the package lists through PackageKit before automatic checks, and when
the window opens with outdated lists.
.TP
.B notify\fR, \fBnotify_security_only
Show a notification for available (security) updates.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/sde/update/
helpers: check.py, model.py, history.py, sources.py, changelog.py, transaction.py
.br
.I ~/.local/state/sde/update-notifier
time of the last automatic check
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkcon (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR sde-suite (1),
.BR apt-get (8)
